{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\n  \"records\": [\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D01-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"417a2e6586fe584fed71c63bca25010559e3be1dede27016c1624f783549ae81\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A5 explicitly seeks acknowledgment that B is asking for A's help.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A3 tests B2's instructions against the leftover door; A5 exploits B4's request to hold it.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 asserts self-sufficiency, but B4 needs practical assistance.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5 turns B4's small request into an admission of dependence.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1's leaning flat-pack cupboard and A3's leftover door establish playable trouble.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5's 'Just to clarify' earns its politeness through B4's reluctant request.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 92\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"That flat-pack cupboard's leaning. I could take a look.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I've got the instructions.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Wonderful. Which page explains that leftover door?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Could you hold it for a second?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Certainly. Just to clarify: you're asking for my help?\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"retained\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A converts a practical request into an explicit admission that B needs A's help.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Displaying competence could resemble D09's pursuit of recognition.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A5 asks whether B needs help rather than asking B to praise A's assembly skills.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"This alternative extracts an admission from physical dependence; the heater alternative bargains over comfort and repair.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Retained after rereading the original: B2 and B4 each supply the next tactic, and the final request precisely pursues D01.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"B4 has already implicitly acknowledged needing help, so A5 heightens explicitness more than practical stakes.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D01-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"8ad07d4c40fece95dc502c0cdf3aceaed011b243759ea72f7872335145f30b4e\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5 offers fuse-box knowledge but never clearly solicits an admission of needing A.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 responds to B2's denial of cold; A5 links B4's blanket request to staying.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 denies discomfort while B4 reveals a concrete wish to keep the blanket.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5 introduces repair expertise but does not increase pressure for acknowledgment.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 supplies a broken heater and jumper, though 'Shall I leave myself?' in A5 is awkward.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A3's withdrawal is economical; A5's phrasing obscures the intended bargaining move.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 69\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"I've brought a blanket. Your heater's still broken?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I'm managing. Leave the blanket, though.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Gladly. Would you say you needed my help?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I need the blanket. I can reset the heater myself.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Of course. The fuse box is in my locked cupboard. Shall I wait while you manage?\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A uses B's practical dependence to seek a spoken admission that A's help is needed.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Trying to remain in someone's company could resemble D02's indirect prevention of departure.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Original A5 ambiguously offers to remain; revised A3 explicitly requests acknowledgment and A5 challenges B4's self-sufficiency.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"The cupboard scene catches an incidental request; this version lets B distinguish needing an object from needing its owner.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Revised within the heater setting to clarify the target admission. Internal reread scores fidelity/logic/relationship/heightening/specificity/wit 5/5/4/4/4/4 = 90; B4's repair claim makes A5's access obstacle consequential. Five spoken turns, under 75 words.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The newly established locked cupboard gives A considerable leverage; actors should preserve sincere helpfulness rather than imply deliberate sabotage.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D02-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"c297150551afc5df51c39788981f7217b5bb7a73e1bc440cc0e8cf0f10afe071\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1, A3 and A5 manufacture food-related reasons to delay departure without asking B to stay.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"B2's salt criticism causes A3's repeat tasting; B4's ten minutes becomes A5's bread timing.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B helps by tasting in B2, then asserts the train deadline in B4.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5 extends a quick taste into waiting until the train's departure time.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1 establishes soup and a departing visitor in one natural request.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5's 'Perfect' sincerely converts B4's obstacle into an invitation.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 92\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Before you get your train, could you taste this soup?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"It needs salt.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"I'll fix that. You'll need to check again.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"My train leaves in ten minutes.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Perfect. That's when the bread comes out.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"retained\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A turns hospitality and B's feedback into successive reasons B must postpone leaving.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Offering attractive food could resemble D10's competition with another plan.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A3 creates an unfinished obligation and A5 adds another delay; A never directly asks B to choose or stay.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"This uses warm hospitality and a timetable; the suitcase alternative uses protective intervention in departure preparations.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Retained after rereading: both partner contributions cause a fresh delay, and the original passes without an invented improvement.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"A5 knowingly overlaps the train's departure, making the emotional need legible but the practical excuse transparent.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D02-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"dc77c0850c91009fab4a9b69644bed59eb486c3eb8df1d1d916ec1efbfadbc1f\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 invents a packing problem and A5 makes settling it a condition of departure.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A3 contests B2 with shoe orientation, but A5 mostly repeats the obstacle after B4.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"B2 corrects the premise and B4 needs to leave, without supplying a specific new constraint.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 2, \"evidence\": \"A5 returns to 'settle the shoes' without increasing the packing problem.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 establishes packing and A3 identifies shoes facing the handle.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A3's shoe complaint is concise, but A5's 'long journey' adds little earned development.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 65\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Before you zip your suitcase, let me wrap that jar of jam.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"It's already wrapped in my jumper.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"That's your train jumper. We'll need to unpack it and find something else.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I'll leave the jam here.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Then you haven't tasted it. I'll get a spoon before you decide.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A makes each attempted departure solution create another small obligation requiring B's presence.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Protective fussing could resemble simply correcting someone's packing.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Original A5 delays departure over shoes; revised A5 abandons packing once B4 solves it and invents a tasting obligation.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"The soup scene extends an existing visit through hospitality; this version converts B's practical escape solutions into new prerequisites.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Replaced the weak shoe dispute with jam packing in the same departure setting. Internal reread scores 5/5/4/4/5/4 = 92: B4 removes the packing issue, causing A5 to switch to tasting. Five spoken turns, under 75 words.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The new jam tasting shares food with alternative a, but the operative tactic is obstructing a solved departure task.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D03-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"0b44411729718360b1e9ba07b068992b6864530f8732783e1582d4c2c02efcf4\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 encourages B's inference; A5 seeks another apology without specifying the actual offense.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 uses B2's mug guess and A5 redirects B4's apology toward something more recent.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"B2 and B4 cooperate, but A5 reveals that the supplied grievance was a decoy.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5 raises the demand from one apology to identifying a further offense.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 establishes a replacement mug, although the actual relational situation remains hidden.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5's 'Keep that tone' efficiently recycles the apology as a starting point.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 77\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"I've put your usual mug out. We can still have tea.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Still? Are you cross with me?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"I'm hoping you won't leave me cross.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I'm sorry. I didn't realise you'd heard.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"I'd only heard one thing. Shall I keep pouring while you cover the rest?\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A signals unresolved hurt and draws out apologies while leaving the offense unnamed.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Vague reproach alone can resemble passive aggression without an actionable apology target.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Original A5 explicitly cultivates an apologetic tone; revised A3 invites repair and A5 expands B4's unsolicited admission.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"This alternative uses familiar hospitality and an accidental revelation; alternative b uses an impending family visit to make reconciliation urgent.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Revised the mug decoy into a tea encounter with a causal revelation. Internal reread scores 5/5/4/4/4/4 = 90; B4 implies undisclosed knowledge, prompting A5 to solicit wider contrition without naming an offense. Five spoken turns, under 75 words.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"A5 briefly approaches information fishing, though its request to 'cover the rest' continues the apology B has begun.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D03-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"33c5bce65c2bbbd2bd3d0c2630a675d4c01083b0e0b6625361386dd39b8794b7\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 hints at reconciliation and A5 nudges B4's concern toward an apology without naming an offense.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 uses B2's ventilation reading; A5 treats B4's question as an opening.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"B4 shows concern, but B2's literal window question mainly feeds the verbal joke.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5 asks B to continue but adds no concrete pressure or consequence.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 2, \"evidence\": \"A1's 'Lovely day' supplies no particular shared activity or relationship.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A3's ventilation line follows B2, but A5 remains a generic encouragement.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 68\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Your parents arrive in ten minutes. I'd like to be able to smile at you.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I thought we'd sorted this out by text.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"You sent a thumbs-up. I couldn't hear any remorse.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I'll send a sad face.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"You're right here. Could you give the sad face a sentence beginning with 'I'?\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A steers B toward a verbal apology by rejecting substitutes while withholding the offense.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Demanding exact wording could resemble treating a procedural detail as the source of legitimacy.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Revised A3 asks for remorse and A5 seeks a spoken sentence because B4 substitutes an emoji; no mark has magical validating power.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative a uses hospitality to draw out more contrition; this version negotiates inadequate repair before the partner's parents arrive.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Introduced an imminent family visit and a prior text exchange. Internal reread scores 5/5/4/4/5/4 = 92; B4's sad-face offer directly causes A5's request to voice it. Five spoken turns, under 75 words.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The final sentence starter strongly indicates the desired wording; it remains character dialogue, but leaves less subtle maneuvering than alternative a.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D04-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"a6f82bb5f420038239101d1ce4761d5d0ff542ac918030b3e614199db4c3102f\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1 seeks approval prospectively, while A5's stump grinder reveals the tree removal is already committed.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 answers B2's improvement question; B4's missing-tree question forces A5's revealing urgency.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 requests scope and B4 checks the tree's whereabouts instead of passively approving.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A5 exposes work already underway while still trying to finish obtaining agreement.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1 establishes a shared garden; A3 and A5 make the pond and tree removal concrete.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5's departing stump grinder economically reveals the concealed timing.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 91\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Would you support a small improvement to the front garden?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"What sort of improvement?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Something with a pond. And no tree.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Where's the tree?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Let's finish agreeing before the stump grinder leaves.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"retained\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A presents a completed intervention as a proposal and pursues approval as its consequences become visible.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Seeking permission before acting would lack the card's essential retrospective timing.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A5's stump grinder makes A1's apparently prospective garden consultation retroactive.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"This alternative conceals a major physical alteration; the dinner scene negotiates capacity while already-invited guests wait.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Retained after rereading: B's search for the tree forces disclosure, and A remains sincerely focused on securing agreement.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The removed tree is inferred through the grinder rather than directly confirmed, and A5 partly evades B4's question.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D04-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"9fdf689e0dedaecdd369744f9efb4017df1756f13cc840ce4f969ef1605b41cb\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1 asks about invitations; A5 reveals that the invited people are already ringing.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 adapts to B2's two chairs; A5 responds to B4's headcount inquiry by prioritizing approval.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 raises limited seating and B4 demands the number of guests.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A5 changes a hypothetical dinner discussion into an immediate doorstep problem.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"B2's two chairs and A5's repeated ringing make the shared-home situation playable.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3's standing-guests proposal follows the actual seating problem in B2.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 91\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"How do you feel about me inviting a few people to dinner?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Tonight? We have two chairs.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"So standing guests would be more considerate?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"How many people?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Could you answer before they ring again?\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"retained\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A bargains for approval of invitations already issued while pretending the decision remains open.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Ordinary event planning would seek agreement before guests were invited.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A5's 'ring again' establishes that A1's invitation proposal concerns an accomplished act.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Unlike the garden's irreversible alteration, this scene uses social embarrassment and limited seating as immediate pressure.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Retained after rereading: the chair objection changes A's offer, and the headcount question precipitates the revealing demand for a quick answer.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"A5 could also follow a different logistical question; its strongest dependency is on B withholding approval.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D05-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"2ad00a1386b073af8894bf02859f2191326c15e500569b8aed164c7df2e8104b\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 recasts eighty place cards as an artistic opportunity and A5 avoids directly assigning them.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"B2's generic thanks adds little to A3; A5 does answer B4's suspicion.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"B4 notices the handoff, but B2 supplies no preference or obstacle for A to exploit.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5 renames the request as artistic impulse without making the task more appealing.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1's elegant bin labels and A3's eighty place cards give actors concrete material.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1's bin-label praise sets up A3's opportunistic artistic commission efficiently.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 70\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"These eighty wedding place cards need names. Your bin labels have better lettering than our invitations.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I like calligraphy. I hate copying guest lists.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"I'd read the names. You'd only do the beautiful part.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Your aunt will complain if I use purple.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"I'll handle my aunt. The ink colour could be entirely yours.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A makes an unwanted writing task attractive by offering B artistic pleasure and removing disliked obligations.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Flattery used to issue a disguised order need not make volunteering appealing.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Original A5 merely denies asking; revised A3 removes copying and A5 protects the colour choice B4 values.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"This version offers creative freedom and protection from criticism; the shed alternative offers control over a repeatedly misused shared space.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Kept the wedding-card setting and praise while giving B actionable preferences. Internal reread scores 5/5/4/4/5/4 = 92; B4's anticipated complaint causes A5's protective offer. Five spoken turns, under 75 words.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"B does not yet volunteer; the scene demonstrates active persuasion and leaves the decision playable.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D05-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"514e75a4d758f0682ad074c1d3ab0fc96449161941a609d749399d490d1b1363\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A3 calls cleaning B's vision, but A5 focuses on ownership of the idea rather than making the task appealing.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A3 uses B2's agreement loosely; A5 responds to B4 by restating the title's premise.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"B4 identifies the unwanted job, but B2 offers only 'It could.'\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 2, \"evidence\": \"A5 supplies no new benefit or commitment after B4 exposes the cleaning request.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 establishes the shed and A3 supplies Saturday as the proposed work time.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A3's promise not to interrupt has character logic; A5 mostly labels the maneuver.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 59\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"You have such a good eye for storage. Sorting our shed could finally give your tools a proper home.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Until you dump paint tins everywhere again.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"You could assign every shelf. I'd follow your labels.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Including a shelf you're forbidden to touch?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Absolutely. You could put it at eye level so I see what I'm missing.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A sells an unwanted organizing task as a chance for B to gain durable control over the shared space.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Making B believe an idea originated with them is narrower than making a task appealing enough to volunteer.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Original A5 asks whose idea it is; revised A3 offers shelf authority and A5 accepts the exclusion B4 proposes.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"The place-card scene trades on artistic pleasure; this version appeals to ownership and relief from A's untidiness.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Kept the shared shed and added B's concrete reason to resist. Internal reread scores 5/5/5/4/4/4 = 93; B4's restricted shelf causes A5 to enlarge the offered control. Five spoken turns, under 75 words.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"A5 accepts a substantial concession, so the humor depends on sincere willingness to pay that price for a voluntary handoff.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D06-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"a66eccdaeaa41b92a86a07df3cb7cbb8989d14e1193194f6fb715bc7b853a380\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 2, \"evidence\": \"A3 volunteers the balcony detail despite the instruction to reveal as little as possible.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A3 uses B2's cake, but A5 asks who used a word that A introduced.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"B4 reasonably investigates A3's disclosure, though B has no further stated stake.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5 retreats after B4's question, increasing suspicion through a largely self-created problem.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 establishes party gossip and B2 supplies a cake incident.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5's 'Nothing confirmed' is compact, but its source question depends on an obvious self-own.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 57\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"When you say you heard about the party, which part?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"The cake went over the balcony. Was that before you left?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Who gave you the timing?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Nobody. Your brother says there's a video.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Have you watched it, or are we both relying on my brother?\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A tests the extent and reliability of B's knowledge while withholding A's own account.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Accidentally confessing through suspicious questions can replace the card's effort to minimize disclosure.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Original A3 supplies the balcony; revised B2 supplies it, while A3 withholds departure timing and A5 checks whether B has seen evidence.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"This alternative probes family gossip and a possible video; the keys scene uses workplace questioning and a witness.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Kept the party, cake and balcony but moved sensitive information to B. Internal reread scores 5/5/4/4/5/4 = 92; B4's video claim causes A5 to test firsthand knowledge. Five spoken turns, under 75 words.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"A5's suggestion of shared reliance may itself be misleading, but it reveals no new incident detail.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D06-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"52343b69fc33b3f314f5cd518f48b7518272c5846afec9236aa170efd1b9523f\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 2, \"evidence\": \"A3 needlessly introduces a drain; A5 stops probing and merely explains the question away.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 tests B2's minimal report and A5 deflects B4's suspicion coherently.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"B4 challenges the suspicious detail, but B2 offers little independent stake.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 2, \"evidence\": \"A5 retreats to a generic briefing explanation without a sharper information request.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 establishes a manager and missing keys; A3 specifies a possible location.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5 is economical but relies on the familiar accidental-disclosure joke created in A3.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 57\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"What did the manager say about the missing keys?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"They might be in the drain. You locked up, didn't you?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Is she asking everyone who locked up, or just me?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Just you. Someone saw you outside.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Did they say what I was doing, or only where I was?\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",